  "why": "the headline measures the move from the FIRST observed ETA, and that first ETA is often left over from a previous port call, so the first revision is large and early; this variant measures the move from the immediately preceding broadcast instead, which is what twin/calibration_fit.py compares. Where the two agree it is because the first crossing of the band is the same broadcast under both bases, and that agreement is computed here rather than assumed",
