 ],
 "honest_limits": "Broadcast ETAs are typed by crews on their own schedule, so a revision here is the earliest the structured stream could have warned; nothing in the recording shows when a carrier would have sent an advisory, so this bounds the advisory channel from above. The first observed ETA is often stale from a previous port call, which makes the first revision large and early and pushes the lead up. Both days are partial and the per-day rate is normalised to the hours actually recorded. The box holds every vessel class, so the cargo-and-tanker cut is reported beside the whole. Moored is a crew-set status, not a berth event."
